p(class="fw5 lh-copy pb3") How can datacenteres keep track of their entire physical and virtual infrastructure without having to context switch between vendors and applications?

p Arkin (VMWare acquired) was a NexusVP funded startup providing datacenters with such a single pane of glass into their entire infrastructure.

p(class="pb3") I helped it over the course of two years move from a interface-less demo to being acquired by VMWare in 2016.

!= partial("../_partials/_post_image", { image: "../assets/images/arkin/dashboard_interface.png", description: "The solution employed a search-first approach, utilizing topology visualizations to delegate complex hierarchies, and a dashboard to render the information-heavy characterstics of a virtualized datacenter." })

!= partial("../_partials/_post_image", { image: "../assets/images/arkin/vxlan_visualization.png", description: "Virtualized datacenters run on new networking concepts that have previously never been visualized. We created many visualizations to augment the traditional networking topologies to help administrators quickly get a sense of their infrastructure. This topology for instance, represents a VxLAN (a virtual successor the traditional LAN) and also provides an interactive guide to how the various components are connected to each other." })

!= partial("../_partials/_post_image", { image: "../assets/images/arkin/icon_set.png", description: "An entire set of new icons was developed to visualize the various components that are part of a virtualized datacenter. We went with solid rectangular icons to denote physical components and circular, hollow icons to represent virtual ones." })

